We will add new methods to client and silo:
`siloBuilder.UseLocalhostClustering(int siloPort = ..., int gatewayPort = ...)` and `clientBuilder.UseLocalhostClustering(int gatewayPort = ...)`

These will configure the system for having a single silo on the local host.

To configure a single silo/client on localhost:
```C#
// on silo
  siloBuilder.UseLocalhostClustering();

// on client
  clientBuilder.UseLocalhostClustering();
```

To configure multiple silos/clients on localhost:
```C#
// on primary
   siloBuilder.UseLocalhostClustering(siloPort, gatewayPort);

// on other silos
  siloBuilder.UseLocalhostClustering(siloPort, gatewayPort, primarySiloEndpoint);

// on client
  clientBuilder.UseLocalhostClustering(gatewayPort1, gatewayPort2, gatewayPort3)
```
